{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-19T00:19:36.461Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1756"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1756: pm context counts in_progress_unowned and in_progress_idle over a different population than in_progress"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Reported in GH-1756 against 2026.11.18. With a custom progress status (workflow.in_progress_status set to doing), the summary's in_progress counts items by the status role, but in_progress_unowned and in_progress_idle count items by the configured progress status. When doing carries the blocked role, pm context reports in_progress 0 alongside in_progress_unowned 2 and in_progress_idle 2, so the advisories exceed their own total. All three counts must describe the same population. The unowned in-progress hygiene and the idle advisory that introduced these counts are related."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["advisories","area:context","gh:1756","in-progress","status-roles"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-19T00:19:36.461Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-19T00:19:36.461Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"For any status-role configuration, in_progress_unowned and in_progress_idle never exceed in_progress; A custom progress status is counted consistently by all three summary fields; Tests cover a custom progress status with the blocked role and with the active role"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-dj98"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"in_progress, in_progress_unowned and in_progress_idle count the same population, so neither advisory can exceed in_progress for any status configuration."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"With a doing progress status whose role is blocked, pm context reports in_progress 0 while in_progress_unowned and in_progress_idle both report 2."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1724","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-19T00:19:36.461Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-w8q4","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-19T00:19:36.461Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"3c318a58b71bee3bf2890eb6e273356074d23475a437f0cebb01008dd94101ca","item_hash_version":3,"message":"File GH-1756","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"7439e32bf34d18bbeb599691c2552c5a8a9464e68e92bdc33419498c09f42f28"}
